  "findings": [
    "Factory PDF page 7 and Zander PDF page 1 agree on host pullups, series resistors and capacitors ahead of D104/T104 input buffers; the cable does not directly drive SIO input pins.",
    "Independent AC impedance checks verify the implemented host passive network against the documented values and declared winding assumptions.",
    "Both ideal and generic transistor driver fixtures pass existing release and load-refinement checks with the host passives. These checks do not qualify absolute buffer voltage limits.",
    "The host network materially changes input extrema. The generic 7406 candidate still produces negative excursions; input clamp behavior and its source-device limits require separate evidence.",
    "Winding parameters, cable capacitance, driver dynamics and missing buffer input loading limit these results; no model calibration or full-board firmware claim follows.",
    "RFT preliminary D104D data permits -0.8 V statically and conditionally -1.5 V negative pulses at no more than 200 ns and 0.5 duty ratio. This differs from applying an SIO limit at the cable.",
    "At the doubled cable load, the generic 7406 candidate violates both conditional negative-pulse amplitude and duration bounds at host buffer inputs despite passing the earlier fixture checks. At nominal load, data pulses satisfy amplitude/duration but duty and model applicability are not established."
  ],
  "nextAction": "Model and constrain D104 input loading/clamps; retain the doubled-load rejection and integrate only an explicitly qualified receiver boundary into firmware checks.",
